From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Artem Butusov <art.sormy@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 18 Nov 2026 00:17:11 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] media: rockchip: rga: Leave a shared interrupt alone while
 suspended

Without the internal MMU the RGA requests its interrupt shared with its
IOMMU, whose interrupts then reach rga_isr while the RGA is runtime
suspended: reading RGA_INT with its clocks off hangs the bus, a hard
lockup at boot. Answer only while the RGA is in use.

Signed-off-by: Artem Butusov <art.sormy@gmail.com>
---
 drivers/media/platform/rockchip/rga/rga.c | 5 +++++
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/media/platform/rockchip/rga/rga.c b/drivers/media/platform/rockchip/rga/rga.c
index fbc9946..00a6322 100644
--- a/drivers/media/platform/rockchip/rga/rga.c
+++ b/drivers/media/platform/rockchip/rga/rga.c
@@ -59,6 +59,10 @@ static irqreturn_t rga_isr(int irq, void *prv)
 {
 	struct rockchip_rga *rga = prv;
 
+	/* A line shared with an IOMMU fires while the RGA, unclocked, cannot be read */
+	if (pm_runtime_get_if_in_use(rga->dev) <= 0)
+		return IRQ_NONE;
+
 	if (rga->hw->handle_irq(rga)) {
 		struct vb2_v4l2_buffer *src, *dst;
 		struct rga_ctx *ctx = rga->curr;
@@ -82,6 +86,7 @@ static irqreturn_t rga_isr(int irq, void *prv)
 		v4l2_m2m_job_finish(rga->m2m_dev, ctx->fh.m2m_ctx);
 	}
 
+	pm_runtime_put(rga->dev);
 	return IRQ_HANDLED;
 }
 
